methods: Methods

A method is a member of its type's C++ struct. A value receiver is a copy (T v = *this;), or
a const reference when the body cannot change it; a pointer receiver is the first parameter
of a static member, T::M(p, args), so no dynamic dispatch is involved. A value method called
through a pointer is p->M(), which checks p for nil and panics like Go. The receiver is
evaluated in Go's order, and a method value (x.M) or method expression (T.M) is a gp::func.

A method called on an interface is different: see gocpp explain interfaces.

Specification: docs/spec/cpp-mapping.md#methods
See also: gocpp explain interfaces, gocpp explain embedding
Also known as: method, receiver, receivers

Example (methods.gp):

    package main

    import "fmt"

    type Acc struct{ total int }

    func (a Acc) Get() int   { return a.total }
    func (a *Acc) Add(n int) { a.total += n }

    func main() {
    	a := &Acc{}
    	a.Add(2)
    	var b Acc
    	b.Add(3)
    	fmt.Println(a.Get(), b.Get())
    }

The C++ that gocpp emit -annotate writes for it:

    //// gpkg/command-line-arguments/pkg.hpp
    // gpkg/command-line-arguments/pkg.hpp: generated by gocpp, do not edit
    #pragma once
    #include <gocpp/rt.hpp>

    namespace gpkg_main {
    struct Acc;

    struct Acc {
        int64_t total = 0;
        bool operator==(const Acc&) const = default;
        std::size_t gp_hash() const {
            return gp::hash_fields(total);
        }
        static constexpr auto gp_fields = gp::fields(gp::field(&Acc::total, "total", false, false));
        int64_t Get() const;
        static void Add(gp::ptr<Acc> a, int64_t n);
    };
    static_assert(sizeof(Acc) == 8 && alignof(Acc) == 8);

    void main();

    } // namespace gpkg_main
    //// gpkg/command-line-arguments/methods.gp.cpp
    // gpkg/command-line-arguments/methods.gp.cpp: generated by gocpp, do not edit
    #include "gpkg/command-line-arguments/pkg.hpp"

    namespace gpkg_main {

    // ---- ./methods.gp:7: func (a Acc) Get() int   { return a.total }
    int64_t Acc::Get() const {
        const Acc& a = *this;
        return a.total;
    }

    // ---- ./methods.gp:8: func (a *Acc) Add(n int) { a.total += n }
    // gp[checks] col 30: p.f through a pointer: -> on a gp::ptr checks for nil and panics like Go
    //     (gocpp build -nochecks removes it)
    void Acc::Add(gp::ptr<Acc> a, int64_t n) {
        a->total = a->total + n;
    }

    // ---- ./methods.gp:10: func main() {
    void main() {

    // ---- ./methods.gp:11: a := &Acc{}
    // gp[refcount] col 7: &T{...} allocates a new reference-counted box that holds the literal
    //     (gp::new_)
        gp::ptr<Acc> a = gp::new_<Acc>(Acc{});

    // ---- ./methods.gp:12: a.Add(2)
    // gp[methods] col 2: pointer method Add: a static call T::Add(p, ...), the receiver pointer is the
    //     first argument; no dynamic dispatch
        Acc::Add(a, 2);

    // ---- ./methods.gp:13: var b Acc
    // gp[boxing] col 6: b is boxed: a pointer-receiver method is called on it, which is (&b).M() and
    //     needs its address
        gp::ptr<Acc> b = gp::new_<Acc>();

    // ---- ./methods.gp:14: b.Add(3)
    // gp[methods] col 2: pointer method Add: a static call T::Add(p, ...), the receiver pointer is the
    //     first argument; no dynamic dispatch
        Acc::Add(b, 3);

    // ---- ./methods.gp:15: fmt.Println(a.Get(), b.Get())
    // gp[interfaces] col 2: fmt.Println: the runtime's gp::fmt functions take each operand with the
    //     descriptor of its Go type (gp::fmt::as), not boxed into an interface first (an operand of a
    //     non-pointer type with an Error method is, see the allocation note)
    // gp[methods] col 14: value method Get through a pointer: p->Get() checks p for nil and panics like
    //     Go (gocpp build -nochecks removes it)
    // gp[order] col 14: gp_t0 holds the result of a call (or a value that a later call could change):
    //     Go evaluates it first, in order, where C++ leaves the order of the operands unspecified
    // gp[methods] col 23: value method Get: a plain member call; the body works on a copy of the
    //     receiver, or on a const reference when it cannot change it
        { auto gp_t0 = a->Get(); gp::fmt::Println(gp_t0, (*b).Get()); }

    // ---- ./methods.gp:16: }
    }

    } // namespace gpkg_main
